<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- One page of the stack: pockets either side of a gap the fixed spine sits in
     (widget_binder.xml), and the arrows that turn the page.
     Every pocket slot a page can hold is here: two rows of two on each side,
     binder_p0 to binder_p3 on the left page and binder_p4 to binder_p7 on the right,
     row by row (BinderLayout.slotOf). A smaller Binder hides the second column and
     row. The pockets live in this one layout, not in nested RemoteViews, because
     Android 11 and 12 only wire a fill in intent's click on views of the item's own
     RemoteViews, and a nested one would never play its book.
     One row Binders put slim arrows either side of the spine: the pages fanned out
     behind show at their top and right edges, so an arrow on the outer edge would
     peek out from every page behind. Taller ones put full size arrows and the page
     number underneath.
     StackView measures a page with AT_MOST, so the first child (a huge image with no
     adjustViewBounds) makes the page take all the room StackView offers. -->
